IMPORT prelude

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore) -- LAYER 1, THE THREE-VALUED HELPERS.
-- Not law: plain functions on the language's own MAYBE BOOLEAN, used by the section modules to combine
-- limbs.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer on these facts" and
-- is never turned into FALSE here.
--   AND: FALSE if either side is FALSE; TRUE if both are TRUE; otherwise NOTHING.
--   OR:  TRUE if either side is TRUE; FALSE if both are FALSE; otherwise NOTHING.
--   NOT: swaps TRUE and FALSE; NOTHING stays NOTHING.
-- A FALSE beats a NOTHING in AND, and a TRUE beats a NOTHING in OR, because one limb that says no (or yes)
-- settles the combination whatever the other limb would say.

GIVEN x IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      y IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`three-valued AND` x y MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN y
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER y
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN x IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      y IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`three-valued OR` x y MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN y
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER y
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN x IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`three-valued NOT` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- A plain fact as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a stated fact` b MEANS
    IF b THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
